---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "../styles/legal.css";

const updated = "24 August 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy policy"
	description="LibertAI privacy policy — what data is processed, why, for how long, and how to exercise your rights."
	path="/privacy-policy"
	lang="en"
	alt="/politique-de-confidentialite"
>
	<section class="legal-page">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="doc">
				<a class="back" href="/">← libertai.io</a>
				<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
				<div class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</div>

				<div class="note">
					<p style="margin:0">
						<strong>English translation.</strong> This page is a translation provided for information only. The French version
						at <a href="/politique-de-confidentialite">/politique-de-confidentialite</a> is the legally binding text.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="toc">
					<a href="#responsable">Controller</a>
					<a href="#principe">Principle</a>
					<a href="#donnees">Data processed</a>
					<a href="#nontraitees">What we do not process</a>
					<a href="#local">Local storage</a>
					<a href="#finalites">Purposes</a>
					<a href="#destinataires">Recipients</a>
					<a href="#transferts">Transfers</a>
					<a href="#durees">Retention periods</a>
					<a href="#droits">Your rights</a>
					<a href="#securite">Security</a>
					<a href="#traceurs">Trackers</a>
					<a href="#modifications">Changes</a>
				</div>

				<h2 id="responsable">1. Data controller</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>Intelligence Artificielle Générale SAS</strong> (“LibertAI”), 76 Promenade des Anglais, 94210 Saint-Maur-des-Fossés,
					France — SIREN 985 392 356.
				</p>
				<p>
					For any question or to exercise your rights:
					<a href="mailto:privacy@libertai.io">privacy@libertai.io</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					A summary of our GDPR commitments — including the data processing agreement available to businesses — is on our
					<a href="/gdpr">GDPR compliance page</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="principe">2. Principle</h2>
				<div class="note">
					<p style="margin:0">
						<strong>LibertAI does not store the content of your exchanges with AI models in a database.</strong> Your requests
						are relayed to the inference servers and the response is then sent back to you; neither the requests nor the responses
						are stored in a database. Only usage counters — number of tokens, number of images, model called, timestamp —
						are retained for billing.
					</p>
				</div>

				<h2 id="donnees">3. Data we process</h2>

				<h3>Account created by email or via Google / GitHub</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>email address and verification status;</li>
					<li>display name and profile picture, where provided;</li>
					<li>identifier and email address provided by the identity provider (Google or GitHub) at sign-in;</li>
					<li>single-use sign-in tokens (“magic links”), stored as a hash and not in plain text.</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Account created with a wallet</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>public wallet address and the network concerned;</li>
					<li>temporary cryptographic challenge used to verify the signature.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>An account created with a wallet contains neither an email address nor any legal identity.</p>

				<h3>Sessions and security</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>refresh token hash, expiry date and revocation date;</li>
					<li>technical information about the device used for the session (client type);</li>
					<li>push notification tokens, platform and app version.</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>API keys</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>name given to the key, creation, expiry and deletion dates.</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Payments and subscriptions</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Payment by card or bank transfer:</strong> customer and subscription identifiers assigned by our payment
						provider, currency, billing periods, plan subscribed to.
						<strong>We neither receive nor store your bank card data</strong> — it is processed exclusively by the provider.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Payment in crypto-assets:</strong> wallet address, transaction reference, block number, amount and status.
						This information is, by its nature, recorded on a public blockchain.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Use of the service</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						per call: API key concerned, number of input and output tokens, number of images, model name, timestamp.
						<strong>Without the content</strong>.
					</li>
					<li>rate-limiting counters, retained ephemerally.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 id="nontraitees">4. What we do not process</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>The content of your conversations and requests</strong> — no storage in a database.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Your IP addresses are not linked to any account</strong>: no table in our database contains an IP
						address field. The IP address is used transiently, in memory, to limit abuse and to determine the display
						currency. Like any online service, our servers and load balancers produce technical logs that may contain IP
						addresses; these are retained for a limited period solely for security and diagnostic purposes.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Your bank card data</strong> — it does not pass through our servers.
					</li>
					<li>We do not use your data to train models, and we neither sell nor rent it to anyone.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 id="local">5. Data stored on your device</h2>
				<p>
					The chat application stores <strong>locally, in your browser</strong>
					and not on our servers: your conversation history and associated attachments, your assistants, projects and memories,
					your generated images, and your display preferences.
				</p>
				<p>
					This data is never transmitted to us. Clearing your browser's site data deletes it permanently — we hold no
					copy of it and cannot restore it.
				</p>

				<h2 id="finalites">6. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Account creation and management, provision of the service</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract — Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Billing, subscriptions, usage accounting</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract and legal obligations — Art. 6(1)(b) and 6(1)(c)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Security, abuse prevention, rate limiting</td>
							<td>
								Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f): protecting the infrastructure against fraud and misuse, and ensuring
								fair access to the service
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Sign-in emails and service-related messages</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract — Art. 6(1)(b)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Aggregated website audience measurement</td>
							<td>
								Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f): understanding traffic in order to improve the service, without
								individual profiling
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Retention of accounting records</td>
							<td>Legal obligation — Art. 6(1)(c)</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<p>
					<strong>Whether the data is required.</strong> Account data is necessary for entering into and performing the contract:
					without it, the service cannot be provided. Any other information you choose to provide, such as a display name,
					is optional and not providing it has no consequence.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Source of the data.</strong> When you sign in via Google or GitHub, we receive your identifier and email
					address from that provider. The billing country is inferred from an IP address geolocation database provided by
					a third party. All other data comes from you or from your use of the service.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Automated decision-making.</strong> No decision producing legal effects concerning you, or significantly
					affecting you, is taken based solely on automated processing. Automated rate-limiting and abuse-prevention mechanisms
					may temporarily restrict access; any lasting suspension of an account is subject to human review and may be challenged
					at the address given in Section 1.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Data protection officer.</strong> No data protection officer has been appointed, as the nature and volume
					of the processing do not require one. Your requests are handled at the address given in Section 1.
				</p>

				<h2 id="destinataires">7. Recipients and processors</h2>
				<p>We use the following providers, each for the purpose indicated:</p>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Provider</th><th>Role</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td>Aleph.IM SAS</td><td>Hosting and confidential computing infrastructure</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Revolut</td><td>Collection of card and bank transfer payments</td></tr>
						<tr><td>thirdweb</td><td>Processing of crypto-asset payments</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Google, GitHub</td><td>Sign-in via identity provider, if you use it</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Email delivery provider</td><td>Delivery of sign-in emails</td></tr>
						<tr><td>MaxMind (GeoLite2)</td><td>Determining the country for currency and VAT purposes</td></tr>
						<tr
							><td>Self-hosted audience measurement</td><td>Traffic statistics for the website and applications</td></tr
						>
						<tr><td>effigy.im</td><td>Generating the profile picture from the wallet address</td></tr>
						<tr><td>CoinGecko</td><td>Crypto-asset prices displayed during a payment</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Base, Solana and Aleph RPC nodes</td><td>Reading and sending on-chain transactions</td></tr>
						<tr>
							<td>jsDelivr, esm.sh</td><td
								>Delivery of components run in the code interpreter and the artifact preview</td
							>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>
					When your browser contacts one of these services, that service technically receives your IP address, as with
					any resource loaded from a third-party domain. None of these calls serves an advertising purpose.
				</p>
				<p>
					The inference servers receive the content of your requests for the time needed to produce the response. When
					you use the built-in web search, your search query is sent to our search service.
				</p>
				<p>
					In the chat application, displaying the icons of the sites cited in search results relies on a third-party
					favicon retrieval service, which therefore receives the domain name of the sites concerned.
				</p>

				<h2 id="transferts">8. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
				<p>
					Some of the providers mentioned above are established outside the European Union, in particular in the United
					States. These transfers are subject to the appropriate safeguards provided for in Chapter V of the GDPR, in
					particular the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
				</p>
				<p>
					Crypto-asset payments are recorded on public blockchains, which are accessible worldwide and by nature cannot
					be modified: this public nature is inherent to the technology and beyond our control.
				</p>

				<h2 id="durees">9. Retention periods</h2>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Data</th><th>Period</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Account and associated data</td><td>Until the account is deleted, or after 3 years without sign-in</td
							>
						</tr>
						<tr><td>Single-use sign-in tokens</td><td>15 minutes, then deleted</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Signature challenges (wallet)</td><td>Deleted upon use</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Sessions</td><td>Until expiry or revocation</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Usage and call counters</td><td>13 months</td></tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Accounting and billing records</td><td>10 years (Article L.123-22 of the French Commercial Code)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr><td>Audience measurement</td><td>13 months maximum</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<h2 id="droits">10. Your rights</h2>
				<p>
					You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, portability and objection,
					as well as the right to withdraw your consent at any time where the processing is based on consent.
				</p>
				<p>
					To exercise them, write to
					<a href="mailto:privacy@libertai.io">privacy@libertai.io</a>. We respond within one month, which may be
					extended by two months for complex requests. We may ask you for information allowing us to verify that the
					request does come from you.
				</p>
				<p>
					Certain data cannot be erased: accounting records, which the law requires us to retain, and transactions
					recorded on a public blockchain, which are technically immutable.
				</p>
				<p>
					Where the processing is based on our legitimate interest, you may
					<strong>object to it at any time</strong> on grounds relating to your particular situation (Art. 21 GDPR), at the
					same address.
				</p>
				<p>
					In accordance with Article 85 of the French Data Protection Act (loi Informatique et Libertés), you may set
					<strong>directives regarding what happens to your data after your death</strong>, and designate a person
					responsible for carrying them out. These directives may be sent to us at
					<a href="mailto:privacy@libertai.io">privacy@libertai.io</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					You may lodge a complaint with the
					<strong>Commission nationale de l'informatique et des libertés (CNIL)</strong>, the French data protection
					authority, 3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07 —
					<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cnil.fr</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="securite">11. Security</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>encryption of data in transit (HTTPS);</li>
					<li>encryption at rest of sensitive authentication tokens;</li>
					<li>storage of session tokens and sign-in codes as irreversible hashes;</li>
					<li>
						authentication cookie inaccessible to the page's JavaScript (<span class="mono">httpOnly</span>),
						transmitted over HTTPS only;
					</li>
					<li>cryptographic verification of notifications from our payment providers;</li>
					<li>
						execution of certain models in a hardware-attested trusted execution environment (TEE); this feature is
						indicated model by model in the interface.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 id="traceurs">12. Cookies and trackers</h2>
				<p>The website and applications set only:</p>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Name</th><th>Role</th><th>Type</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td>libertai_auth</td><td>Maintaining your session</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
						<tr>
							<td>oauth_state</td><td>Protection of sign-in via Google / GitHub</td><td>Strictly necessary</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>oauth_redirect</td><td>Return to the original page after sign-in</td><td>Strictly necessary</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>preferred_instances</td><td>Routing continuity for inference calls</td><td>Strictly necessary</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>sidebar_state</td><td>State of the side panel</td><td>User convenience, requested by the user</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>
					The display theme and your conversation data are stored in the browser's local storage, not in cookies. Crypto
					wallets that you connect may also write their own technical keys to this local storage.
				</p>
				<p>These trackers are essential to the operation of the service and do not require your consent.</p>
				<p>
					Audience measurement for the website and applications is provided by a
					<strong>self-hosted solution, without advertising cookies and without cross-site tracking</strong>. The data
					is strictly statistical, is not cross-referenced with other processing and is not shared with any third party.
					As such, it falls within the consent exemption provided by the CNIL for audience measurement.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong
						>No advertising cookies, no social network pixels and no third-party behavioral measurement trackers</strong
					> are set. Calls to the technical services listed in Section 7 are used neither for profiling nor for cross-site
					tracking.
				</p>

				<h2 id="modifications">13. Changes</h2>
				<p>
					This policy may be updated. The date at the top indicates the latest revision; in the event of a substantial
					change, users with an account will be informed.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<Footer lang="en" variant="legal" />
</Base>
